The "Wire up Tavily/Exa/Marginalia/Mojeek: README, POD, env, Changes" commit (584e8a4) updated .env.example with TEST_WEBSEARCH_TAVILY_API_KEY / TEST_WEBSEARCH_EXA_API_KEY / TEST_WEBSEARCH_MARGINALIA_API_KEY / TEST_WEBSEARCH_MOJEEK_API_KEY comments, documenting that these vars should gate live-test subtests the way every other provider (Brave, Serper, Google, Yandex, Reddit OAuth, SearxNG) has in t/50-live.t. But t/50-live.t itself was never updated — grep for tavily|exa|marginalia|mojeek in that file returns nothing. So the four new providers have no live-test path at all, despite .env.example implying one exists.

